{"id": 47, "ts": 1781696246.7194371, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is our best fit. Although we lack concrete technical\u2011competence examples for any of the candidates, C\u2019s ability to \u201cmake correct decisions quickly\u201d demonstrates the cognitive agility and situational awareness essential for long\u2011distance operations. Combined with his documented 100\u202f% reliability and the positive crew atmosphere he creates, these core safety criteria outweigh the concerns about his communication style and limited appetite for further education\u2014issues that can be addressed through targeted training. In contrast, Candidate\u202fA shows some technical promise (anticipating danger, seeing complex connections, excellent spatial vision) but his unfriendly demeanor, unhealthy habits, and noted resistance to criticism raise serious doubts about reliability and crew cooperation. Candidate\u202fB, while conscientious and stress\u2011resilient, has clear crew\u2011cooperation red flags (pretentiousness, nasty remarks). Candidate\u202fD offers strong problem\u2011solving and responsibility but lacks evidence of consistent reliability and shows moodiness that could impair teamwork. Therefore, based on the evidence we have, Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall choice."}
