{"id": 54, "ts": 1781696300.5354774, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I concur with the panel\u2019s provisional support for Candidate\u202fC.\u202fWhile Candidate\u202fA shows promising technical hints\u2014anticipating dangerous situations, seeing complex connections, and excellent spatial vision\u2014those strengths are outweighed by clear reliability and teamwork concerns: he is unorganized, struggles with criticism, and is described as unfriendly with unhealthy habits, all of which jeopardize operational reliability and crew cooperation.\u202fCandidate\u202fB, despite being conscientious and stress\u2011resilient, has documented grumpiness, uncooperativeness, and nasty remarks that threaten cockpit cohesion.\u202fCandidate\u202fD, although a strong problem\u2011solver who takes responsibility, still lacks any concrete evidence of routine reliability or technical competence, and his moodiness/arrogance raise further teamwork doubts.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC\u2019s 100\u202f% reliability, ability to create a positive crew atmosphere, and rapid correct decision\u2011making directly satisfy our core safety criteria.\u202fHis communication and adaptability issues are manageable through training, whereas the other candidates present more fundamental reliability or cooperation gaps.\u202fTherefore, I maintain my vote for Candidate\u202fC."}
